Hand 1
https://tinyurl.com/2d4nnb8q
qx|A1|st||rh||ah|Board 1 IMPs   -   On November 20, 2024|pn|hondo717,asiring,vs_bbo,marikaSz|
md|3SKJ95HK92D76CQ532,SA3HAQJ764DKCKJ86,SQ764HT3DAQ9432C4,ST82H85DJT85CAT97|sv|0|
mb|2D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Some players won't open a Weak-2 with an outside 4-card major as North did. But I think that is an unnecessary restriction. Even here, where we have a 4-4 spade fit, diamonds in our 6-2 fit is a much better spot, although it doesn't work here.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@H is a bit of an underbid. It probably still doesn't get E/W to 4@H, but I think a better bid by West is 3@H. That is NOT a preempt. You never preempt over a preempt. 3@H shows a strong hand with very nice hearts. |
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Another possibility, as suggested, is to double and correct to 3@H. But that also probably doesn't get them to 4@H that they will make. Simply, it is a difficult hand to bid.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


