nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|H6|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally leading doubletons is not a particularly good lead. But here the other alternatives are not that good either. A diamond is out of the question. Had we not bid clubs, then leading clubs would be okay. West could lead a trump but that could give away a trick. Therefore, by the process of elimination a heart is okay here.|
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|sk|s|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If spades are 3-2, at best, I will likely take 3 spades, 1 diamond ruff, 2 clubs and 3 hearts for 9 tricks. And taking the spade finesse probably can't hurt so long as spades are not 4-1.|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


