UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with the way declarer played the hand except for the first trick. There was no need to play the @SK. Playing @ST was better. At worst makes no difference and could often result in a 2nd spade trick. Other than that, drawing trump and setting up clubs is the best way to play the hand.|
PG| ***** 50 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I also agree with West pass. My competitive guidelines say you should only bid ^*B3 over 3^*n if:
^Ca) you have a 9 card fit; or
^Cb) you have a singleton, particularly in their suit. West has neither and is vulnerable.|
PG| ***** 51 ***** |
PG| ***** 52 ***** |


