Hand 5 TO 4
https://tinyurl.com/27dxuwrv
qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   On November 20, 2024|pn|hondo717,vs_bbo,marikaSz,aspiring|
md|3ST9752HA82DQ95C43,SAJ8643HKQD82CJ86,SKQHJ94DAJ3CA9752,SHT7653DKT764CKQT|sv|n|
mb|1N|mb|2D|an|Diamonds and a higher suit|
PG| ***** 54 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I like the 2@D |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dont,DONT^*N|CP||FP||at| bid showing diamonds and either hearts or spades with at least 5-4.|
PG| ***** 55 ***** |


mb|P|mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now, normally West would pass with 3 diamonds or else bid 2@H asking partner to pass with hearts or correct to spades. However, given West has 6 spades his bid is not clear. It is very unlikely that East has spades. One possibility is for West to bid 2@H, since the hearts are better than the spades and hope East has 5 hearts.|
PG| ***** 56 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Another possibility is for West to bid 2@S and hope for the best. This is fairly rare in DONT and simply says West want to play in spades. On average East will have 1-2 spades so it is unclear what West should bid.|
PG| ***** 57 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With a better spade suit (say 3 honors or 2 honors and more intermediates) 2@S is best. But, here it is somewhat of a guess and I am not sure what I would bid.|
PG| ***** 58 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^B@2^*BWest: ^*NWith known position of Diamonds, although very small why not just pass?|
PG| ***** 59 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Because partner might have 4 diamonds. Admittedly partner might have 5 diamonds and 4 hearts. In the final analysis 2@H has more upside.|
PG| ***** 60 ***** |


mb|2H|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
